WEBVTT

00:21.750 --> 00:27.470
<i>If you could turn back time, 
is there somewhere you'd want to return?</i>

00:40.590 --> 00:41.790
<i>There is for me.</i>

00:49.180 --> 00:51.820
I am so blind

00:51.820 --> 00:53.820
Still running

00:54.100 --> 00:57.040
Running out of sight

00:57.040 --> 00:58.690
In the night

00:58.690 --> 01:01.200
I'm feeling goosebumps

01:02.570 --> 01:09.670
Betting against the odds again,
I'm being swayed like in a dance

01:09.670 --> 01:14.340
No more Blah Blah Bluff-filled Table

01:15.950 --> 01:17.830
Just tell me how to figure it out

01:17.830 --> 01:19.640
Inside my head, I'm painting the town

01:19.640 --> 01:20.850
Addition is affliction

01:20.850 --> 01:21.720
Something's missing

01:21.720 --> 01:23.540
(Oh you really got me wrong)

01:23.540 --> 01:25.400
I wanna get out so I'm taking a chance

01:25.400 --> 01:26.260
I gotta advance

01:26.260 --> 01:27.450
You know who I am?

01:27.450 --> 01:28.900
I'm a trickster

01:29.770 --> 01:31.360
Just take a chance

01:31.360 --> 01:32.530
Play the game

01:32.530 --> 01:34.530
It sounds insane

01:34.530 --> 01:37.700
Fate smiles at the borderline

01:37.700 --> 01:44.040
Rather than dance to someone else's tune,
I wanna dance to my own.

01:44.040 --> 01:46.000
Yea I'm moving like that

01:46.000 --> 01:47.300
Give it a try

01:47.300 --> 01:48.420
Keep on going down

01:48.420 --> 01:51.100
I just need something real

01:51.100 --> 01:54.670
Then we need no fakes

01:54.670 --> 01:58.930
I'll let my soul be wild and free

02:17.480 --> 02:19.010
We're here!

02:20.260 --> 02:21.910
Let's go, Michel.

02:22.280 --> 02:23.750
I don't feel too well...

02:24.210 --> 02:25.270
I'll stay here.

02:25.270 --> 02:27.040
What's wrong? You get car sick?

02:27.040 --> 02:30.460
You're the one who wanted 
to come to the amusement park.

02:30.460 --> 02:31.540
I'm staying here.

02:33.920 --> 02:35.710
Here we go.

02:35.710 --> 02:38.200
Take a look over there, Michel.

02:38.200 --> 02:40.100
That's the Ferris wheel.

02:40.100 --> 02:42.550
It's <i>way</i> taller than I am.

02:42.790 --> 02:45.070
I see it. It's goes so high!

02:45.070 --> 02:49.190
From up there, you get 
a crystal clear view of all around.

02:49.190 --> 02:51.690
I'm sure you'll feel lots better.

02:52.200 --> 02:53.860
I wanna go!

02:53.860 --> 02:54.940
Tch.

02:56.830 --> 02:58.890
Chris, we're gonna leave you.

02:58.890 --> 03:01.320
Hey, wait up!

03:02.490 --> 03:04.870
<i>My father, Tyler, was cheerful and loved kids.</i>

03:05.730 --> 03:09.250
<i>Michel was always frail, but she used
to be stronger than she is now.</i>

03:10.110 --> 03:12.070
<i>We lost my mother early on,</i>

03:12.070 --> 03:14.540
<i>but the three of us were so happy together</i>

03:14.540 --> 03:17.370
<i>that we could forget the sorrow sometimes.</i>

03:20.390 --> 03:22.640
<i>A slightly burned but warm meal.</i>

03:23.700 --> 03:25.660
<i>A card game we all enjoyed.</i>

03:26.540 --> 03:30.200
<i>Back then, I knew what a real smile was.</i>

03:31.390 --> 03:34.020
Chris, we're gonna leave you behind!

03:36.040 --> 03:37.180
Chris!

03:37.180 --> 03:38.870
Just a little longer!

03:43.150 --> 03:44.030
<i>However...</i>

03:45.540 --> 03:47.910
Chris! Chris!

03:47.910 --> 03:50.360
Stay with me, Chris!

03:51.640 --> 03:58.310
<i>The things things you assume will stay with 
you forever are more fragile than they seem.</i>

04:10.550 --> 04:11.810
Dad?

04:19.420 --> 04:21.100
<i>We lost our father that day.</i>

04:21.100 --> 04:26.320
<i>It left me and my little sister
all alone in the world.</i>

04:27.550 --> 04:29.260
<i>And another me was born.</i>

04:30.930 --> 04:33.410
<i>A smooth talker with a pretty face</i>

04:33.410 --> 04:35.690
<i>and the aroma of sweet things around him...</i>

04:35.690 --> 04:37.330
<i>Always laughing like a fool.</i>

04:38.310 --> 04:43.830
<i>I hide and suppress my heart as 
I handle tough jobs with a smile.</i>

04:44.140 --> 04:47.080
<i>I do it to protect myself.</i>

04:48.430 --> 04:51.470
<i>To protect the one place I wish to return.</i>

04:55.240 --> 05:00.230
<i>I've forgotten my true
 emotions along the way, but...</i>

05:01.140 --> 05:02.480
<i>X-Blind.</i>

05:03.140 --> 05:05.110
<i>It's my one-in-a-million chance.</i>

05:05.480 --> 05:07.620
<i>Please listen carefully.</i>

05:08.030 --> 05:11.240
<i>Your sister is...</i>

05:13.230 --> 05:17.340
<i>I think I was meant to live for this moment.</i>

05:18.790 --> 05:20.500
<i>What my father did...</i>

05:21.630 --> 05:26.130
<i>It left us with deep sorrow 
and pain that won't go away.</i>

05:27.230 --> 05:28.010
<i>But...</i>

05:33.030 --> 05:34.020
You, Finn...

05:35.320 --> 05:40.770
You're the spitting image of the version
 of myself I abandoned long ago.

05:42.900 --> 05:48.530
Lying to you feels like
 lying to myself back then.

05:49.710 --> 05:51.710
That's why I didn't want to do it.

05:52.510 --> 05:54.290
I didn't want you to know.

05:57.150 --> 06:00.120
No... I can't turn back time.

06:01.130 --> 06:04.520
It only moves forward.

06:23.180 --> 06:25.820
Oh, good. You're awake.

06:27.910 --> 06:30.430
Why am I alive?

06:30.430 --> 06:31.450
Finn!

06:33.580 --> 06:34.940
Answer me, Finn!

06:34.940 --> 06:36.450
Where did Chris go?!

06:36.450 --> 06:37.960
What is he up to?!

06:38.190 --> 06:39.800
How much do you know?!

06:39.800 --> 06:41.330
What's all this about?

06:46.730 --> 06:49.970
He took the cards and disappeared.

06:49.970 --> 06:51.290
Chris did?

06:51.630 --> 06:52.760
He got the jack of clubs?!

06:53.230 --> 06:55.510
No, that one's safe.

06:55.510 --> 06:56.520
Huh?

06:56.820 --> 07:00.770
Aya herself got in touch with us.

07:01.430 --> 07:07.400
It seems Chris fled after 
incapacitating the two of you.

07:08.260 --> 07:12.030
X-Playing Cards cannot 
be destroyed by anyone.

07:12.240 --> 07:14.780
But with skill like his...

07:15.140 --> 07:18.380
He aimed for the pocket with the card.

07:18.810 --> 07:20.840
He took the 5 of clubs.

07:24.680 --> 07:27.080
Chris has been dismissed from High Card

07:27.080 --> 07:29.160
and put on the wanted list
by order of the president.

07:29.640 --> 07:30.800
Hey, Leo.

07:31.030 --> 07:33.800
Do you want to find Chris on our own first?

07:34.200 --> 07:37.510
We can ask him what he's trying to pull.

07:37.510 --> 07:38.180
No.

07:39.090 --> 07:44.520
Vijay and Wendy are already on 
another job at Fourland Palace.

07:45.850 --> 07:51.570
I'm going to join them now as personal
 protection for the king and princes.

07:52.120 --> 07:54.570
That is High Card's current mission.

07:54.570 --> 07:55.820
And you're okay with that?

07:55.820 --> 07:59.080
Chris is High Card's responsibility, isn't he?

07:59.080 --> 08:00.590
Don't you think so, Leo?!

08:00.590 --> 08:01.210
That's the problem.

08:02.050 --> 08:04.120
We're too close to Chris.

08:04.510 --> 08:06.220
That's why the higher-ups decided this.

08:06.220 --> 08:08.090
And it especially applies to you, Finn.

08:10.110 --> 08:13.210
Pinochle will keep your card
 for the time being.

08:13.940 --> 08:15.340
President's orders.

08:15.940 --> 08:19.030
Owen is conducting an investigation on Chris.

08:19.030 --> 08:20.100
Owen?

08:20.100 --> 08:23.480
He never says no to the president.

08:26.660 --> 08:28.580
Let me give you a little quiz.

08:28.580 --> 08:31.730
What do you think is at 
the end of this tunnel?

08:35.680 --> 08:37.990
Don't take it too seriously.

08:38.230 --> 08:39.860
I don't know the answer either.

08:40.910 --> 08:44.220
Is there a light at the end of the darkness?

08:44.220 --> 08:46.630
Or does the darkness continue?

08:46.630 --> 08:48.880
Perhaps it's a dead end.

08:49.480 --> 08:53.940
Whatever the case, we won't know
unless we move forward.

08:54.510 --> 08:58.890
And so I proceed. That's all there is to it.

08:59.700 --> 09:01.240
Sorry, guys.

09:01.630 --> 09:06.020
There is no "turning back" 
in the Klondike dictionary.

09:07.170 --> 09:08.710
To family!

09:08.710 --> 09:10.220
To family!

09:16.950 --> 09:18.250
Did you find him?

09:18.250 --> 09:19.420
Yes.

09:19.420 --> 09:22.410
I don't agree with your plan, though.

09:30.020 --> 09:30.870
Hey.

09:31.170 --> 09:33.250
Sorry to bother you so early in the morning.

09:34.030 --> 09:35.460
Just off the night shift, right?

09:35.830 --> 09:38.380
Here's what you asked for.

09:38.380 --> 09:40.310
And the other thing?

09:43.450 --> 09:45.870
You sent me this out of the blue.
 What are you up to?

09:45.870 --> 09:47.060
That's a secret.

09:47.750 --> 09:49.580
Thanks for holding on to it.

09:49.960 --> 09:50.560
Huh?

09:50.810 --> 09:53.350
Tell me the truth.

09:54.620 --> 09:57.580
The police came to the pub last night.

09:57.580 --> 10:00.450
They said they were looking
for you on brass's orders.

10:01.620 --> 10:03.560
Because I'm so popular.

10:13.210 --> 10:15.210
What's with those injuries?

10:16.060 --> 10:18.700
Are you getting into something dangerous?

10:18.700 --> 10:20.970
Without telling any of us?

10:21.710 --> 10:23.860
If you're not going to answer me, then fine.

10:23.860 --> 10:25.600
I have my ways.

10:25.600 --> 10:26.430
Play!

10:44.130 --> 10:46.970
You're attractive when you're not talking.

11:02.340 --> 11:03.650
Welp...

11:03.650 --> 11:05.680
I've got a date to keep.

11:05.680 --> 11:06.220
Huh?!

11:06.220 --> 11:07.770
Don't mess with me!

11:11.290 --> 11:14.430
Chris Redgrave, come with me to the station.

11:14.750 --> 11:16.690
I've got a lot of questions for—

11:16.690 --> 11:16.980
What?

11:17.630 --> 11:19.610
Brass's orders.

11:19.610 --> 11:20.610
Nothing personal.

11:20.990 --> 11:22.910
Brass, huh?

11:24.240 --> 11:25.030
Huh?!

11:25.030 --> 11:25.990
What are you doing?!

11:28.370 --> 11:29.220
Chris!

11:29.220 --> 11:30.510
It's dangerous! Come with me!

11:34.180 --> 11:36.000
Be a good boy and come on out.

11:45.390 --> 11:46.760
You!

11:47.310 --> 11:48.820
You're with the Klondikes...

11:49.640 --> 11:50.640
Go.

11:50.830 --> 11:52.160
Huh.

12:07.690 --> 12:09.770
I'm sorry, but we're closed for—

12:11.880 --> 12:13.620
Hello, Finn.

12:22.750 --> 12:23.720
Read this.

12:28.490 --> 12:31.000
"To Finn's greatest family..."

12:32.110 --> 12:37.480
"This may not amount to much, but use 
it to rebuild Sun Fields Orphanage."

12:38.550 --> 12:40.310
"Sincerely, Finn's tutor."

12:41.350 --> 12:45.190
I received it along with this.

12:49.180 --> 12:50.240
Chris...

12:50.980 --> 12:52.310
This is my fault.

12:52.820 --> 12:55.780
If I hadn't gone to Sun Fields that day...

12:56.310 --> 12:58.290
If I weren't working this job...

12:59.070 --> 13:01.000
I ruined everything.

13:01.640 --> 13:04.650
You even told me it'd be 
better if I never came back.

13:06.070 --> 13:09.660
You always blame yourself.

13:10.150 --> 13:11.450
That's a bad habit, you know?

13:15.490 --> 13:19.630
I was going to tell you the truth about 
your past when the time was right.

13:20.540 --> 13:21.550
I...

13:22.710 --> 13:25.380
I think I might have hurt you.

13:25.830 --> 13:26.530
I'm sorry.

13:27.010 --> 13:29.030
Don't be, Lindsey...

13:29.030 --> 13:31.190
Finn, listen to me carefully.

13:31.910 --> 13:37.170
I know Sun Fields was your beloved home.
A place for you to return to.

13:37.850 --> 13:41.040
The house may be gone, but I'm still here.

13:41.590 --> 13:45.050
So is Sam and everyone else, 
all because you protected us.

13:45.940 --> 13:50.330
As long as we're still your family, 
Sun Fields will always be there for you.

13:52.710 --> 13:55.810
I did say I wished you'd move on, though.

13:56.440 --> 13:57.860
And that's how I feel.

13:58.220 --> 14:04.070
Everyone eventually finds a new place
 to belong and leaves Sun Fields.

14:05.190 --> 14:11.700
Seeing you all leave the nest is 
part of my job as an adult, you know?

14:12.840 --> 14:15.970
You don't need to have just one home, Finn.

14:16.650 --> 14:18.850
Adults are complicated.

14:18.850 --> 14:22.990
You have to get what goes into what they 
say in order to get your head around 'em.

14:22.990 --> 14:24.210
What's that mean?

14:24.690 --> 14:26.210
You'll understand when you grow up.

14:30.310 --> 14:32.050
Thanks, Lindsey.

14:34.170 --> 14:37.320
I mean, they pay me well,
I can take all the joyrides I want,

14:37.320 --> 14:39.370
and the old man's tea is good.

14:39.370 --> 14:42.180
I guess this <i>is</i> a place 
I like coming back to.

14:44.170 --> 14:46.930
I'm sure the others all feel the same way,

14:46.930 --> 14:50.490
including Chris, the guy who wrote this.

14:51.000 --> 14:55.230
Does that mean he's part of your family now?

14:56.140 --> 14:58.860
Family? Who knows.

14:58.860 --> 15:04.250
He bosses me around as my mentor, he's a 
womanizer, and he's always joking around.

15:04.860 --> 15:07.640
But, yeah, he's my...

15:10.650 --> 15:16.260
Well, he has a sister by blood named Michel.

15:19.260 --> 15:20.770
Family...

15:21.060 --> 15:22.020
What's wrong?!

15:22.020 --> 15:25.400
Chris...

15:25.400 --> 15:27.150
Chris is going to die!

15:27.560 --> 15:31.910
Tyler played a hand of four cards...
 at the cost of his own life.

15:32.570 --> 15:34.410
He took the 5 of clubs.

15:35.070 --> 15:37.160
There's no way. Chris can't be...

15:37.390 --> 15:39.290
That stupid idiot!

15:39.290 --> 15:40.200
Finn?

15:48.910 --> 15:50.800
<i>Chris, you...</i>

15:51.400 --> 15:56.940
<i>Finn, I was your mentor, 
so we did everything together.</i>

16:02.120 --> 16:05.790
<i>That's right. Chris went alone that time...</i>

16:06.450 --> 16:07.730
<i>At the auction, too.</i>

16:08.180 --> 16:10.360
Looks like we'll have to change the plan.

16:10.530 --> 16:13.030
C'mon, Finn says he can do it.

16:13.200 --> 16:14.500
Why don't we trust him?

16:14.950 --> 16:17.950
<i>And this last card...</i>

16:21.860 --> 16:25.900
<i>I'd hoped I wouldn't be
 with you for the final card.</i>

16:27.090 --> 16:30.920
<i>But it was all for family. 
I'm sure you'll understand.</i>

16:30.920 --> 16:33.700
<i>With the four cards you've collected...</i>

16:38.280 --> 16:39.720
<i>It won't be long now, Michel.</i>

16:40.430 --> 16:41.680
Chris!

16:41.930 --> 16:44.420
You idiot!

16:46.520 --> 16:49.000
<i>Your big brother is coming to save you.</i>

16:55.950 --> 16:58.630
<i>Are you that worried about Finn and Chris?</i>

16:59.290 --> 17:00.580
<i>I am not!</i>

17:01.090 --> 17:05.210
I'm sure those two will be waiting 
for us at Old Maid Street.

17:05.530 --> 17:07.420
I said I'm not worried!

17:07.420 --> 17:09.340
<i>It's me. Do you read me?</i>

17:09.810 --> 17:10.810
Sir?!

17:10.810 --> 17:12.460
<i>Just give me the facts.</i>

17:12.870 --> 17:16.120
Has Prince Noah left the room?

17:16.120 --> 17:17.290
<i>N-No.</i>

17:18.690 --> 17:20.620
Is there a problem?

17:23.410 --> 17:24.380
What was that?

17:37.630 --> 17:38.740
Play!

17:39.450 --> 17:40.460
Play!

17:41.310 --> 17:42.080
Play!

17:46.150 --> 17:48.000
So you came to catch Chris?

17:48.260 --> 17:51.110
But shooting on sight...

17:51.110 --> 17:53.380
Crazy things are happening in this city.

17:53.380 --> 17:55.880
Yet the truth remains hidden.

17:56.710 --> 18:00.810
I want to catch him and uncover
 what's really going on here.

18:00.810 --> 18:01.890
<i>Urgent!</i>

18:01.890 --> 18:04.470
<i>Gunfire reported at 
the Royal Hospital of Premiera.</i>

18:04.470 --> 18:08.250
<i>Suspect is male. About 180 centimeters tall.
Dark hair. Dressed in a biker jacket.</i>

18:43.330 --> 18:44.470
<i>Hey, Finn.</i>

18:44.900 --> 18:47.180
<i>I should've known you'd 
be the first to arrive.</i>

18:47.740 --> 18:48.790
Chris...

18:49.800 --> 18:52.980
Not even I thought this would 
really work in the beginning.

18:53.590 --> 18:58.530
Because I'm a High Card, and my job 
is to collect the cards, you know?

19:00.340 --> 19:06.080
It wasn't until I encountered the player 
with the 5 of spades and obtained his card.

19:07.090 --> 19:09.330
And by the next one, I'd made up my mind.

19:10.470 --> 19:14.690
In addition to the one Leo prepared,
 I had a second dummy card.

19:14.690 --> 19:16.990
So I got the real 5 of diamonds.

19:18.440 --> 19:22.090
The Klondikes ended up with the second dummy.

19:23.020 --> 19:26.850
In order to lure the 5 of clubs 
onto the train to Polostick,

19:26.850 --> 19:29.350
I used a hostesses from his favorite club.

19:30.230 --> 19:32.230
Leaking our whereabouts,

19:34.110 --> 19:37.360
kicking you off the train
while pretending to help you,

19:37.900 --> 19:42.740
and shooting you, who happened 
to witness the pivotal moment...

19:43.390 --> 19:47.490
I did it all to collect these four cards.

19:48.060 --> 19:52.850
You know what happens if you play
 a four-card X-Hand, don't you?

19:53.300 --> 19:55.000
Why didn't you tell me anything?

19:56.090 --> 19:57.880
You're like I used to be.

19:59.850 --> 20:02.170
<i>Seeing you smile so genuinely...</i>

20:02.980 --> 20:06.390
<i>It felt like watching my old self.</i>

20:07.380 --> 20:12.660
<i>Like it would strip off 
all the masks I'm wearing.</i>

20:12.660 --> 20:14.900
If you'd told me, I could have helped—

20:14.900 --> 20:17.020
We're just colleagues.

20:18.010 --> 20:18.850
<i>Right?</i>

20:20.730 --> 20:23.910
Rebuild the orphanage
 and live with your family.

20:24.510 --> 20:28.190
<i>That's the least I can help with 
to atone for what I've done.</i>

20:30.630 --> 20:34.040
<i>You're wrong... You got it all wrong, Chris.</i>

20:34.780 --> 20:39.050
"Family" isn't just who 
you're related to by blood.

20:39.770 --> 20:45.890
Eating together, working together, 
laughing together, crying together...

20:46.120 --> 20:48.100
<i></i>That's<i> family!</i>

20:48.100 --> 20:49.640
<i>The people you want to return to!</i>

20:50.010 --> 20:53.140
I've finally found where I belong.

20:53.140 --> 20:55.260
You're not just a colleague!

20:55.260 --> 20:59.150
We have to go home to Old Maid, 
where the rest of High Card...

20:59.490 --> 21:01.500
your family is waiting!

21:04.670 --> 21:07.090
You want to go back... together?

21:10.610 --> 21:11.650
Sorry.

21:12.430 --> 21:15.190
This is my first and last chance 
to save my little sister.

21:15.980 --> 21:16.860
Chris!

21:16.860 --> 21:17.670
Don't die!

21:17.910 --> 21:21.250
<i>Hey, Chris? Chris!</i>

21:21.250 --> 21:23.320
<i>Wait! Answer me, Chr—</i>

21:21.830 --> 21:23.090
See you, Finn.

21:31.610 --> 21:32.870
Chris!

21:36.440 --> 21:37.150
Don't—

21:42.510 --> 21:46.280
Right now, I'm an immortal ladies' man!

21:50.750 --> 21:52.040
You...

21:52.380 --> 21:53.890
Finn Oldman.

21:53.890 --> 21:56.620
You disobeyed instructions to stand by,

21:56.620 --> 22:00.040
not to mention obstructed a
 direct order from Master Theodore.

22:00.550 --> 22:02.220
I cannot disregard this any longer.

22:03.250 --> 22:05.050
You're fired.

22:05.070 --> 22:09.300
We move on, kicking away a crisis

22:09.300 --> 22:16.720
Dare to cause a dramatic upset

22:18.670 --> 22:23.430
To those of you in the safe zone
who hate to rock the boat

22:23.430 --> 22:26.870
Over here, I'm barely surviving today

22:26.870 --> 22:29.180
In exchange for my MP

22:29.180 --> 22:32.760
I can't cool down this burning passion

22:32.760 --> 22:36.730
Bring it, weak-ass monsters!

22:36.730 --> 22:40.200
With that said, my knees are shaking

22:40.200 --> 22:42.790
But I still dream on

22:42.790 --> 22:46.860
Because I don't want to make myself a liar

22:46.860 --> 22:50.710
(Are you all ready?)

22:49.470 --> 22:51.560
And don't be afraid

22:51.560 --> 22:53.410
Let's get sassy

22:53.410 --> 22:56.700
I'm sharpening the senses I lost

22:56.700 --> 23:00.720
Repeating a desperate act to get in the zone

23:01.630 --> 23:05.930
We move on, welcoming any phenomenon

23:05.930 --> 23:12.120
I challenge myself on the lifeline I run on

23:12.120 --> 23:15.680
Please let it slide if I take a huge tumble

23:15.680 --> 23:20.600
I smile as I go, dedicating my whole life

23:20.600 --> 23:23.440
That's why I get serious

23:23.440 --> 23:25.690
So I can leave my tracks

23:25.690 --> 23:31.910
Shake up the destiny in my hand

23:36.370 --> 23:38.730
Next time: "FINN."
